              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aedicula, aediculae — \"a shrine, a small temple; a niche\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "In compitō aedicula parva est, et viātōrēs ibi flōrēs pōnunt. At the crossroads there is a small shrine, and travellers put flowers there."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "First declension, feminine: aedicula, aediculae f., a diminutive of aedēs. A little shrine, or a niche for a statue."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "aedicula is a diminutive of aedēs 'temple, house' (Lewis & Short), made with -cula. English keeps aedicule in architecture."
            }
          ]
        },
