          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "exstruō, exstruere — \"to build up, to raise, to pile up\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Cīvēs novam porticum in forō exstruunt. The citizens put up a new colonnade in the forum."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "exstruō, exstruere, exstrūxī, exstrūctum. Also to pile up: mēnsās epulīs exstruere, to load tables with food."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "exstruō is built from ex- 'up, out' and struō 'to pile up, to build' (EtymDB; Lewis & Short). English construct and structure come from struō."
            }
          ]
        },
